{
  "_comment": [
    "HTMLHint rules for the desktop GUI's HTML.",
    "",
    "Enabled rules cover the structural mistakes a browser quietly",
    "papers over: a duplicated id, an unclosed tag, a missing alt.",
    "Those are exactly the faults that turn into a subtly wrong screen",
    "rather than an error anybody would notice.",
    "",
    "id-class-value is off on purpose. Most field ids are built from the",
    "simulation parameter they carry -- field-m_rate, stat-G_ST,",
    "field-initial_allele_count -- so the GUI can map a control to its",
    "config key by name. Renaming them to please a casing rule would",
    "break that mapping to buy nothing.",
    "",
    "href-abs-or-rel and link liveness are off here as well: whether a",
    "link points at a file that exists is checked by",
    "dev/bin/check-webui-assets, which can actually look on disk."
  ],
  "tagname-lowercase": true,
  "attr-lowercase": true,
  "attr-value-double-quotes": true,
  "attr-no-duplication": true,
  "attr-unsafe-chars": true,
  "doctype-first": true,
  "doctype-html5": true,
  "tag-pair": true,
  "tag-self-close": false,
  "spec-char-escape": true,
  "id-unique": true,
  "src-not-empty": true,
  "head-script-disabled": false,
  "style-disabled": true,
  "inline-style-disabled": false,
  "inline-script-disabled": false,
  "space-tab-mixed-disabled": "space",
  "id-class-ad-disabled": true,
  "href-abs-or-rel": false,
  "title-require": true,
  "alt-require": true,
  "input-requires-label": false,
  "empty-tag-not-self-closed": false,
  "id-class-value": false
}
